          {
            title: 'Tuong',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tuong (TÆ°á»›ng) is a Vietnamese climbing/shedding card game closely related to Tiáº¿n LÃªn (Thirteen). 4 players, 52-card deck, 13 cards each. 2 is highest. Goal: shed all cards first. Singles, pairs, triples, straights, double-sequences all valid. 'Bombs' (four-of-a-kind, long double-sequences) can beat 2s.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tuong (Tướng) belongs to Vietnam's national climbing-card tradition. The closely related game Tiến Lên (Go Forward) is considered the national card game of Vietnam and shares the same shedding-and-climbing family as Zheng Shangyou and President. The genre spread beyond Vietnam, including to the USA after the Vietnam War where it is sometimes known as Thirteen or Viet Cong.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards. Rank: 2(high)-3(low). Suits: â™¥>â™¦>â™£>â™ .',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '13 each (4 players). 3â™  holder starts.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'No twos in sequences: Twos cannot be used in sequences; straights run from 3 up to ace only.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Stacking: When all but one have passed, the last player to play may continue with successively higher combinations of the same type until unable.',
                  },
                ],
              },
